{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_literal_type", "label": "Literal type", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A type inhabited by exactly one value \u2014 'pending', 42, true. In a union it is the main modelling tool: autocompletion, typo errors, and narrowing."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_as_const", "label": "as const", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On a literal expression: every property becomes readonly and every literal keeps its type. On an array it produces a readonly tuple. Applies only to literals, not computed values."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_derived_union", "label": "Derived union from as const list", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "const STATUSES = [...] as const; type Status = (typeof STATUSES)[number]. One runtime list; the type updates when an entry is added."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_satisfies", "label": "satisfies vs as const", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "satisfies checks against a type without replacing the inferred one. An annotation would widen; as const alone would not check. Use it for computed values that as const cannot wrap."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_as_vs_as_const", "label": "as const is not as T", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "as const asks for the narrowest inference of something already written and cannot lie. as T asserts a type the compiler cannot verify."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_as_const", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_literal_type", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_as_const", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_01_primitives_and_inference_widening", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_as_const", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_03_arrays_and_tuples_tuple_type", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/02-literal-types-and-as-const.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_02_literal_types_and_as_const_derive